-- title:
--   Level and tame-inertia laws on the invariant chart
-- statement:
--   Throughout, write $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ for `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ for `GaloisField q 2`, $A_0 := A.\mathrm{comap}(k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q})$ for the valuation subring of $k_0$ obtained by pulling $A$ back along the inclusion of $k_0$, and $\kappa_0$, $\kappa$ for the residue fields of $A_0$ and of $A$.
--
--   *Global data.* A prime $q$; a nonzero natural number $M'$; a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; a finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'$ over $\kappa$, that field being the $\kappa$-subfield of $\kappa((t))$ generated by the $q$-expansions $j$ and $j(M'\cdot)$; a hypothesis `hle` that the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field is contained in the base change of the $X_H$ function field of level $q^2M'$ with $H = \mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$; a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ on the former field with values in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'$ (that is, a valuation subring of the source together with a surjective residue map onto the target whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ and its residue map, and a degree-preserving, divisor-compatible map on places); and a distinguished element $s \in W$.
--
--   *Base-field and uniformiser data.* An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$; an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ together with `hπ` asserting $\pi_0 \in A$; a natural number $\ell$; elements $\zeta_0, \varpi_t \in k_0$; an intermediate field $K_b$ of $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ and `hAb` asserting that $x \in A_b$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $A$; and an element $\varpi_b \in A_b$.
--
--   *Auxiliary-level chart data.* A prime $\ell'$; an element $\xi \in k_0$; an intermediate field $K_\ell$ of $k_0 \subseteq k_0((t))$, carrying an $A_0$-algebra structure compatible with the $k_0$-structure; a nonzero element $j_\ell \in K_\ell$; an element $\varpi_t' \in A_0$; an ideal $y$ of $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K_\ell\,j_\ell$, the $A_0$-subalgebra of elements of $K_\ell$ integral over $A_0[j_\ell]$; an $A_0$-subalgebra $\tilde B$ of $K_\ell$ (`Bt`) and a valuation subring $\tilde W$ of $K_\ell$ (`Wt`) with `hBW` asserting $\tilde B \subseteq \tilde W$; a natural number $n$; an element $\gamma_0 \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$; a $k_0$-automorphism $\tau_0$ of $K_\ell$; a natural number $m$; an element $\zeta_c$ of the adic completion of $A_0$ at its maximal ideal; a hypothesis `hjK` that the $q\ell'$-th power $q$-expansion of $j$ over $k_0$ lies in $K_\ell$; an element $a_0 \in A_0$; and a finite set `ends` of subrings of $K_\ell$. Finally, a bundle $\mathcal F$, an element of the structure [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.RigidDescentHyps`](def/ModularCurve_RigidDescentHyps.html#L28) applied to exactly the data listed so far, whose fields constrain that data as a rigid chart at the auxiliary level $q\ell'$.
--
--   *The hypothesis `hInert` (rigid-level reduction with level and tame-inertia laws).* For every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa_0$ there is a ring homomorphism $\tilde\rho : \tilde B \to \mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa_0$, the Drinfeld coordinate ring $\kappa_0[X_0,X_1]/(\mathrm{drinfeldPoly}\,q\,\kappa_0 - 1)$, such that: $\tilde\rho$ is surjective; $\tilde\rho\,b = 0$ if and only if $b$, viewed in $\tilde W$, lies in the maximal ideal of $\tilde W$; $\tilde\rho$ sends $a \in A_0$ to the image of the residue of $a$ in $\kappa_0$; and the following two laws hold. (Level law.) For every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $k_0$-automorphism $\tau$ of $K_\ell$ satisfying $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,(q\ell')\,((q\ell')^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}(q\ell')M')\,\gamma^{-1}\,K_\ell\,\tau$ — that is, $\tau$ implements on ratios of $q$-expansions of modular forms for $\Gamma_H((q\ell')^2M')$ the translation by the matrix $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell')\,\gamma^{-1}$, normalised through any embedding $k_0 \hookrightarrow \mathbb C$ sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell')}$ — and preserving $\tilde W$ ($f \in \tilde W \iff \tau f \in \tilde W$), there exists $c \in \mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c)$ in $\mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$, the kernel of the character $(g,c) \mapsto \det(g)\,c^{q+1}$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Z/q) \times \mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$, such that $\tilde\rho(\tau b) = \mathrm{hAction}\,q\,\kappa_0\,(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c)(\tilde\rho\, b)$ whenever $b \in \tilde B$ and $\tau b \in \tilde B$; moreover $c \neq 1$ if $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity; and the same scalar $c$ is linked to the identity matrix, in the sense that there are $\gamma' \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and a $k_0$-automorphism $\tau'$ of $K_\ell$, level-attached to $\gamma'^{-1}$ in the above sense and preserving $\tilde W$, with $(1,c) \in \mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$ and $\tilde\rho(\tau' b) = \mathrm{hAction}\,q\,\kappa_0\,(1,c)(\tilde\rho\,b)$ for all $b \in \tilde B$ with $\tau' b \in \tilde B$. (Tame-inertia law.) For every $\pi \in A_0$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$, every pair of ring automorphisms $\sigma_L$ of $k_0$ and $\sigma_A$ of $A_0$ compatible under $A_0 \hookrightarrow k_0$ and congruent to the identity modulo the maximal ideal of $A_0$, every $\tilde\alpha \in A_0$ with $\sigma_A \pi = \tilde\alpha\pi$, every $\alpha \in \mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$ whose image in $\kappa_0$ is the residue of $\tilde\alpha$, and every ring automorphism $\tau$ of $K_\ell$ acting on Laurent series coefficientwise by $\sigma_L$: $\tau$ maps $\tilde B$ into itself and satisfies $f \in \tilde W \iff \tau f \in \tilde W$, and for every $d \in (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ whose image in $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ is $\alpha^{q+1}$, with $(\mathrm{diagOneElem}\,q\,(d^q)^{-1}, \alpha^q) \in \mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$, one has $\tilde\rho(\tau b) = \mathrm{hAction}\,q\,\kappa_0\,(\mathrm{diagOneElem}\,q\,(d^q)^{-1}, \alpha^q)(\tilde\rho\,b)$ for all $b \in \tilde B$ with $\tau b \in \tilde B$, where $\mathrm{diagOneElem}\,q\,e$ is the diagonal matrix $\mathrm{diag}(1,e)$.
--
--   *Descent naming block.* A subgroup $G$ of the group of $k_0$-automorphisms of $K_\ell$ with `hG` asserting that $G$ is the closure of the set of those $\tau$ for which some $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ makes $\tau$ level-attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ in the above sense; an intermediate field $K_0$ of $k_0 \subseteq K_\ell$ with `hK₀` asserting $K_0 = \mathrm{fixedField}\,G$; an $A_0$-subalgebra $B_0$ of $K_\ell$ with `hB₀` asserting that $f \in B_0$ if and only if $f \in \tilde B$ and $\tau f = f$ for all $\tau \in G$; and a valuation subring $W_0'$ of $K_0$ with `hW₀'` asserting that $f \in W_0'$ if and only if the image of $f$ in $K_\ell$ lies in $\tilde W$.
--
--   *Conclusion.* For every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$ and every proof that $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa$ is a domain, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the group $\mu_{q+1}(\mathbb F_{q^2})$ of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity and a ring homomorphism
--   $$\rho : B_0 \longrightarrow \mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s,$$
--   the target being the subfield of the Drinfeld function field $\mathrm{Frac}(\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa)$ fixed by the subgroup generated by the automorphisms $\mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}\,q\,\kappa\,(1,\zeta)$ for $\zeta \in C_s$, such that all of the following hold.
--
--   (1) $\#C_s = 2\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$, where $\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$ is $\mathrm{jWidthChar}\,q$ of the value of $j$ at the place $s$ divided by $\mathrm{placeRamificationJ}\,M'\,s$, the order at $s$ of $j$ minus that value, and $\mathrm{jWidthChar}\,q\,j$ equals $12$ or $1$ for $q = 2$ according as $j = 0$ or not, $6$ or $1$ for $q = 3$ likewise, and $\mathrm{jWidth}\,j$ otherwise.
--
--   (2) $\ker\rho$ is the principal ideal of $B_0$ generated by the image of $\pi_0$, regarded as an element of $A_0$ via `hπ`.
--
--   (3) For every $a \in A_0$, $\rho$ of the image of $a$ in $B_0$ is the image in $\mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ of the residue in $\kappa$ of $a$ viewed as an element of $A$.
--
--   (4) Every $z \in \mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ is a ratio of values of $\rho$: there are $g,h \in B_0$ with $\rho h \neq 0$ and $z\,\rho h = \rho g$.
--
--   (5) An element $z$ of $\mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ lies in the range of $\rho$ if and only if its image in the Drinfeld function field lies in the range of the structure map from $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa$.
--
--   (6) (Level law, with trivial scalar.) For every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, every $k_0$-automorphism $\tau$ of $K_\ell$ level-attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ at level $q\ell'$ in the sense of $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}$ as above, every proof that $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$ lies in $\mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$, and every $f \in B_0$ with $\tau f \in B_0$: the image of $\rho(\tau f)$ in the Drinfeld function field equals $\mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}\,q\,\kappa\,(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ applied to the image of $\rho f$. No condition relating $\tau$ to $\tilde W$ is imposed here.
--
--   (7) (Tame-inertia law.) For every $\pi \in A_0$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$, every pair of ring automorphisms $\sigma_L$ of $k_0$ and $\sigma_A$ of $A_0$ compatible under $A_0 \hookrightarrow k_0$ and congruent to the identity modulo the maximal ideal of $A_0$, every $\tilde\alpha \in A_0$ with $\sigma_A\pi = \tilde\alpha\pi$, every $\alpha \in \mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$ whose image in $\kappa$ is the residue of $\tilde\alpha$ viewed in $A$, and every ring automorphism $\tau$ of $K_\ell$ acting on Laurent series coefficientwise by $\sigma_L$: $\tau$ maps $B_0$ into itself, and for every $d \in (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$ whose image in $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ is $\alpha^{q+1}$, every proof that $(\mathrm{diagOneElem}\,q\,(d^q)^{-1}, \alpha^q)$ lies in $\mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$, and every $f \in B_0$ with $\tau f \in B_0$, the image of $\rho(\tau f)$ in the Drinfeld function field equals $\mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}\,q\,\kappa\,(\mathrm{diagOneElem}\,q\,(d^q)^{-1}, \alpha^q)$ applied to the image of $\rho f$.
--
--   This is the descent step from the rigid chart at auxiliary level $q\ell'$ to the chart of invariants $B_0 = \tilde B^G$ over the base valuation ring: the single reduction map onto the invariant subfield of the Drinfeld (Deligne–Lusztig) function field carries simultaneously the $\Gamma_0(M')$-level law and the tame-inertia law, so that the two actions are read on one and the same reduction. It feeds the construction of the supersingular charts of the semistable model in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart), where the special fibre at level $q$ is identified in terms of Drinfeld curves.
